ull,"archived":false,"disabled":false,"open_issues_count":3124,"license":{"key":"other","name":"Other","spdx_id":"NOASSERTION","url":null,"node_id":"MDc6TGljZW5zZTA="},"allow_forking":true,"is_template":false,"web_commit_signoff_required":false,"topics":["linter","python","typechecker","types","typing"],"visibility":"public","forks":3065,"open_issues":3124,"watchers":20064,"default_branch":"master","permissions":{"admin":false,"maintain":false,"push":false,"triage":false,"pull":true}},"body":"On certain situations with circular imports, some of the types defined on the circular import are not available, even as a comment/forward reference:\n\n``` python\n# bar.py\nfrom typing import Union\n\nimport foo\n\nMyType = Union[int, str]\n\n# foo.py\nimport bar\n\nx = \"\"  # type: bar.MyType\n```\n\nIf I have these two files,  then I get:\n\n```\n$ mypy bar.py\nbar.py:3: note: In module imported here:\nfoo.py:3: error: Invalid type \"bar.MyType\"\n```\n\n(Note that this isn't a \"MyType is an undefined name error, it's an \"Invalid type\"). I was expecting the bar.MyType reference to be possible.\n\nThis structure is quite similar to the one in #1972 (and came from the same piece of code), these issues might be related\n","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/python/mypy/issues/1984/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/python/mypy/issues/1984/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":"completed"}},"event":"cross-referenced"},{"id":745857240,"node_id":"MDEyOkxhYmVsZWRFdmVudDc0NTg1NzI0MA==","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/python/mypy/issues/events/745857240","actor":{"login":"gnprice","id":28173,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI4MTcz","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/28173?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/gnprice","html_url":"https://github.com/gnprice","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/